# Security & Config

- Never hardcode API keys, DB passwords, or channel credentials — use env vars only.
- Local: `.env.local` (gitignored). Production: hosting env / secret store — same code, different vars.
- Known env vars (extend as features land):

| Variable | Used by |
|----------|---------|
| `DB_USER` | Oracle pool |
| `DB_PASSWORD` | Oracle pool |
| `DB_CONNECT_STRING` | Oracle pool |
| `AUTH_SECRET` | NextAuth (Day 2+) |
| `EMAIL_*` / `RESEND_API_KEY` | EmailChannel (Day 6+) |

- No patient PII (name, phone, email, notes) in logs or `console.log`.
- No secrets in client bundles — only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` for non-sensitive public config.
